hat acute viral neuroinflammation does not uniformly accelerate amyloid all surfaced as caveats. Reinforced existing neuroinflammation content cross-chapter (ch19 chronicity, ch08, ch09 glial-NfL/GFAP, ch18) with the exposure-defined precedent, and re-qualified the ch09 "glial inflammation without overt neurodegeneration" framing. Phase 6: citation insertions only (incoming cert 0.56 → no bumps per Evidence Quality Floor 0.40–0.59); Phase 11 adversarial review re-calibrated the claim certainty 0.56→0.42 (analogical-distance factor: acute florid encephalitides are far from chronic low-grade contested ME/CFS neuroinflammation). No treatment claims, no new mechanisms asserted directly in ME/CFS. _Motivated by:_ @Aditi2026EncephalitisDementia (primary TriNetX cohort); @Granerod2017PostEncephalitis (independent UK replication). _Clinical relevance:_ MEDIUM — cross-disease mechanistic precedent for causal-hierarchy and long-term-sequelae framing; reinforces rationale for long-term cognitive monitoring but non-actionable (no ME/CFS dementia data). _Quality note:_ none (targeted cross-disease integration, evidence-quality floor respected, adversarial review converged).

## Version 7.15

- *Fatigue as a core symptom: definition, severity, fatigability, and phenotype structure* ([Chapter 3, new `sec-00-fatigue` (sec-aggregator + 4 subsecs: definition, severity, objective measurement, phenotypes; 9 content environments — 2 clinical-findings + 1 ICF clinical-finding + 1 achievement severity benchmark + 2 clinical-findings (actigraphy, central fatigability) + 1 open-question (subjective-objective) + 2 hypothesis (embedded clusters, severity subgroups) + 1 clinical-finding (differentiation biomarker) + 1 synthesis `syn:fatigue-not-unitary`); hypothesis registry, 3 new entries (2 H + 1 OQ); `bib/diagnosis-assessment.bib`, 10 new entries; Appendix H, 10 new annotated sections; glossary.json, 1 new entry (Fatigability)]): Integrated fatigue as a standalone core symptom distinct from the PEM relationship already covered in `sec-01-pem`. Established that fatigue is the most prevalent and among the most quantitatively severe core symptoms — pooled severity 77.9/100 across 60 RCTs (n=7,088) with physical and cognitive fatigue exceeding mental (~74 vs 70) @Park2024fatigueSeverity — and that the subjective perception (fatigue, ICF b1300) is formally distinct from objective performance decline (fatigability, ICF b4552) @Tankisi2024fatigueFatigability @BileviciuteLjungar2020ICF. Added objective correlates: actigraphy-measured reduced activity and blunted rhythms in CFS vs 63,133 controls with a genetic-continuity signal @Liu2025geneticFatigueActigraphy, and a central (brain-level) failure of motor drive rather than peripheral muscle exhaustion on MRI/EEG/EMG @Bedard2026centralFatigability. Added phenotype structure: fatigue is embedded within Brain/Gut-Immune/Autonomic symptom clusters rather than a unitary factor @HabermannHorstmeier2025symptomClusters, four severity subgroups whose structure depends on case definition @EatonFitch2026registryQoL, and a preliminary EV-miRNA signature distinguishing ME/CFS fatigue from idiopathic chronic fatigue and depression (very early, n=6, must replicate) @Eguchi2026EVmiRNAfatigue. Added a synthesis (`syn:fatigue-not-unitary`) and an open question on whether subjective fatigue and objective fatigability dissociate. Two hypotheses carry explicit falsifiable predictions (pre-registered cluster×treatment interaction trial; independent-cohort k-means replication with external-measure thresholds). Design/treatment: none (clinical-symptom topic). _Motivated by:_ an 10-paper corpus on fatigue definition/severity/fatigability/phenotype. _Clinical relevance:_ HIGH — objective fatigability + severity benchmarks inform clinical assessment and trial design; severity applicability for severe/very-severe patients is explicitly flagged as not stratified by the included evidence. _Quality note:_ none (PROCEED; 0/10 papers <0.40 discounted; no treatment claims; no certainty bumps).

## Version 7.14

- *Fatigue–PEM relationship: PEM as a multi-system cascade distinct from simple fatigue, and the conditional feasibility of PEM without fatigue* ([Chapter 3, `sec-01-pem`, subsec-01 definition-characteristics (1 achievement + 2 envs) + subsec-02 physiological-basis (2 speculations + 1 open-question + 1 synthesis); hypothesis registry, 6 new entries; `bib/diagnosis-assessment.bib`, 14 new entries; Appendix H, 14 new annotated sections; glossary.json, 2 new entries]): Integrated the definitional evidence that post-exertional malaise is a multi-system symptom cascade that extends beyond simple fatigue — meta-analytically highly discriminating (OR ~10.4), an independent factor separable from cognitive and sleep domains, with a multi-faceted fatigue component — and that case definitions differ sharply (Fukuda fatigue-centric/PEM-optional vs CCC/ICC/IOM PEM-required). Developed the previously untested question of whether PEM can occur without fatigue across three temporal cases (crash window, onset, near-normal baseline fatigue) and five candidate mechanisms (dominant-channel expression, two-factor PEM substructure, trigger-type dependence, labeling/measurement frame, self-report-vs-objective dissociation). All PEM-without-fatigue content is rigorously confined to candidate-hypothesis status: since no study directly tests fatigue-absence, the null reading (apparent fatigue-absence is always a measurement or labeling artifact) is the explicit epistemic default until within-subject data exist, with falsifiable two-criterion predictions (free-text fatigue-absence vs zero-fatigue-under-direct-probing). Reinforced the ch02 ICC case-definition account with `@Lim2020caseDefinitions` and `@Brown2020metaPEM`. Design/treatment: none. _Motivated by:_ @IOM2015redefining (PEM as hallmark, SEID), @Brown2020metaPEM (OR 10.4), @Conroy2023empirical (factor analysis, n=2,308), @McManimen2019deconstruct (two-factor PEM fatigue), @Stussman2025selfReport (self-report vs objective PEM gap) — an 14-paper corpus documenting PEM as a construct distinct from fatigue. _Clinical relevance:_ HIGH — PEM-predominant, low-fatigue patients may be missed if fatigue is treated as the only required marker; clinicians should elicit multi-system post-exertional worsening. _Quality note:_ WEAK-EVIDENCE applies to the PEM-without-fatigue development sub-column (indirect/analogical support, capped at certainty 0.45); the definitional core is not weak-evidence.

- *Striatal dopaminergic dysfunction in Long COVID: added functional ME/CFS imaging and treatment evidence + reconciled citations* ([Chapter 9, `sec:neurotransmitters`, subsec-01; hypothesis registry, 1 entry reinforced; `bib/neuroinflammation.bib`, `bib/long-covid.bib`, 2 new bib entries @Inderyas2026DopaminergicFC @Pokharel2025SARS2SNpc; appendix H, 10 new annotated entries]): Retroactive-strengthen of the prior VMAT2-PET/Long-COVID dopamine integration. Added the first functional evidence in an *actual ME/CFS cohort* — Inderyas et al. 2026 ultra-high-field 7T fMRI showing altered resting-state connectivity in dopamine-associated striatal circuits (nucleus accumbens) in ME/CFS and Long COVID — which extends the dopaminergic-signaling finding beyond the SARS-CoV-2-triggered subset, and cited the Young et al. 2025 solriamfetol (dual NE-DA reuptake inhibitor) RCT in ME/CFS as preliminary treatment-response support. Updated the existing VMAT2 observation, dopaminergic-convergence synthesis, and generalizability open-question in ch09 with these citations, disaggregating the support into functional-imaging (0.55) / treatment-response (0.45) components distinct from the Long-COVID structural certainty (0.72). Reinforced the registry hypothesis "Striatal Dopaminergic Terminal Loss as Cross-Condition Pathology in Post-Infectious ME/CFS" (certainty retained at 0.25, with rationale that functional evidence supports circuit involvement but not structural terminal-loss probability). Added Pokharel et al. 2025 (SARS-CoV-2 substantia nigra invasion, animal model) as mechanistic support for DA-neuron tropism. Reconciled a bib duplicate: removed redundant `Young2025SolriamfetolMECFS` key, enriched the canonical `@Young2025solriamfetol` entry. Direct structural VMAT2-PET data in ME/CFS remain absent and are not over-claimed. _Motivated by:_ @Liu2026VMAT2longcovid (Liu et al., eBioMedicine 2026 VMAT2-PET study) and the 2026-08-10 ScienceAlert report of the same finding. _Clinical relevance:_ MEDIUM — mechanistic context for dopaminergic-augmentation treatment directions and a candidate objective-biomarker (VMAT2-PET) research program. _Quality note:_ none (retroactive reinforcement; no new hypotheses, no new treatment recommendations).

