- *Peppercorn 2025 DNA methylation landscapes in ME/CFS vs Long COVID + methylation consolidation gap-fill* ([Chapter 14d cross-disease, 1 new speculation `spec:methylene-mecfs-longcovid-distinguish`; Chapter 14 global-methylation, 1 citation + cross-reference reinforcement; Appendix H, 1 new annotated entry; `bib/genetics-epigenetics.bib` 1 entry corrected (DOI/PMID/volume/pages + accurate DMF counts); hypothesis-registry.typ, 1 new entry]): Gap-filled the partially-integrated Peppercorn et al.\ 2025 (IJMS) comparison of the peripheral-blood methylomes of ME/CFS and Long COVID, which was previously cited only for its 67.8% hypermethylation-dominance statistic. Added a cross-disease speculation (ch14d) that the PBMC methylome has a largely shared core between the two conditions (118 shared differentially methylated fragments, Pearson R = 0.88) yet contains distinguishing sites (ME/CFS 214 DMFs vs Long COVID 429; 6 opposite-direction DMFs incl. an FGD2 promoter hypermethylated only in LC), with a stage-from-onset confound explicitly flagged (LC ~1 yr vs ME/CFS ~12 yr) (cert 0.52) — consistent with the existing "shared yet distinct" ME/CFS-vs-LC narrative (cf.\ 7T MRS) and a caution against pooling the two conditions in methylation research. Retroactive adaptation (Phase 6) added the Peppercorn RRBS study and a cross-reference to the new speculation in the ch14 global-methylation section. Corrected the bib placeholder DOI (`10.3390/ijmsXXXXX`) to the verified `10.3390/ijms26146631` and updated the note to the accurate 214/429/118 DMF figures (145 hyper / 69 hypo in ME/CFS). No certainty bumps (single-lab n=5 study, raw cert 0.52, no independent replication — below the bump bar). _Motivated by:_ @Peppercorn2025methylation — the Otago head-to-head RRBS methylome comparison providing the first direct ME/CFS-vs-Long-COVID methylation landscape. _Clinical relevance:_ MEDIUM — a research-stage differential-diagnostic/stratification direction (if the 6 opposite-direction DMF